@[[f9bc0948-7487-4985-b10c-55e5a4169729]] 116/120, final 4. Moves route STILL has the old top-level code after four verdicts — this time do a literal string replacement, nothing else. Replace:

const { reference, table_id, starts_at_local, party_size } = req.body;
...the whole `if (!reference)` 422 block...

with:

const moves = req.body.moves;
if (!Array.isArray(moves) || moves.length === 0) return 422 validation_failed "Missing moves array".
const moved = [];
for (const m of moves) {
  const r = getReservationByReference(m.reference);
  if (!r) return 404 not_found;
  const t = restaurant.tables.find(t => t.id === m.table_id);
  if (!t) return 404 not_found;
  r.table_id = m.table_id;
  if (m.starts_at_local !== undefined) r.starts_at_local = m.starts_at_local;
  if (m.party_size !== undefined) r.party_size = m.party_size;
  moved.push(serializeReservation(r));
}
return 201 { reservations: moved }.

DST, exact calibration (your last attempt compared mismatched formats): const dt = DateTime.fromISO(input, { zone }); invalid = !dt.isValid || dt.toFormat("yyyy-MM-dd'T'HH:mm") !== input. Only then 422 invalid_local_time. Dedupe availability slots by dt.toMillis(). Overlaps by epoch millis.

Rebuild, your suite, revision + counts. This closes stage 1.

